1
00:00:04,462 --> 00:00:05,505
Run.

2
00:00:08,842 --> 00:00:10,301
I'm the Doctor, by the way. What's your name?

3
00:00:10,427 --> 00:00:13,096
- Rose. - Nice to meet you, Rose. Run for your life!

4
00:00:19,269 --> 00:00:20,854
It's gonna follow us!

5
00:00:20,937 --> 00:00:23,314
The assembled hoards of Genghis Khan couldn't get through that door,

6
00:00:23,398 --> 00:00:24,774
and believe me, they've tried.

7
00:00:24,858 --> 00:00:27,068
- Are you alien? - Yes.

8
00:00:30,989 --> 00:00:32,073
You could come with me.

9
00:00:32,157 --> 00:00:34,409
- Is it always this dangerous? - Yeah.

10
00:00:41,458 --> 00:00:43,918
Right, Rose Tyler, you tell me, where do you wanna go?

11
00:00:44,002 --> 00:00:48,298
Backwards or forwards in time? It's your choice. What's it gonna be?

12
00:00:49,841 --> 00:00:51,009
Forwards.

13
00:00:55,805 --> 00:00:58,600
- How far? - One hundred years.

14
00:01:09,277 --> 00:01:12,447
There you go! Step outside those doors, it's the 22nd century.

15
00:01:12,614 --> 00:01:14,157
- You're kidding. - That's a bit boring, though.

16
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:15,325
Do you wanna go further?

17
00:01:15,492 --> 00:01:16,659
Fine by me.

18
00:01:24,834 --> 00:01:27,253
Ten thousand years in the future.

19
00:01:27,337 --> 00:01:31,674
Step outside, it's the year 12005. The new Roman Empire.

20
00:01:31,758 --> 00:01:33,635
You think you're so impressive.

21
00:01:33,718 --> 00:01:35,887
- I am so impressive. - You wish!

22
00:01:36,221 --> 00:01:39,724
Right, then. You asked for it. I know exactly where to go.

23
00:01:43,228 --> 00:01:44,437
Hold on!

24
00:02:00,286 --> 00:02:02,038
Where are we?

25
00:02:04,582 --> 00:02:06,334
What's out there?

26
00:02:37,407 --> 00:02:41,619
You lot... You spend all your time thinking about dying.

27
00:02:41,703 --> 00:02:46,416
How you're gonna get killed by eggs or beef or global warming or asteroids.

28
00:02:47,083 --> 00:02:49,961
But you never take time to imagine the impossible.

29
00:02:50,044 --> 00:02:51,796
That maybe you survived.

30
00:02:54,132 --> 00:02:57,969
This is the year 5.5/Apple/26.

31
00:02:58,052 --> 00:03:00,138
Five billion years in your future.

32
00:03:00,847 --> 00:03:02,765
And this is the day...

33
00:03:02,974 --> 00:03:04,392
Hold on...

34
00:03:11,608 --> 00:03:13,735
This is the day the sun expands.

35
00:03:15,653 --> 00:03:18,031
Welcome to the end of the world.

36
00:04:09,707 --> 00:04:12,794
Shuttles five and six now docking.

37
00:04:13,878 --> 00:04:15,880
Guests are reminded that Platform One

38
00:04:15,964 --> 00:04:19,676
forbids the use of weapons, teleportation and religion.

39
00:04:20,677 --> 00:04:23,680
Earth-death is scheduled for 15:39,

40
00:04:23,763 --> 00:04:26,641
followed by drinks in the Manchester Suite.

41
00:04:27,392 --> 00:04:30,228
So when it says "guests", does that mean people?

42
00:04:30,311 --> 00:04:31,771
Depends what you mean by people.

43
00:04:31,854 --> 00:04:34,732
- I mean people. What do you mean? - Aliens.

44
00:04:35,608 --> 00:04:38,653
What are they doing on board this spaceship? What's it all for?

45
00:04:38,736 --> 00:04:41,823
It's not really a spaceship, more like an observation deck.

46
00:04:41,906 --> 00:04:44,951
The great and the good are gathering to watch the planet burn.

47
00:04:45,034 --> 00:04:46,661
- What for? - Fun!

48
00:04:50,540 --> 00:04:54,294
Mind you, when I say "the great and the good", what I mean is the rich.

49
00:04:54,377 --> 00:04:59,090
But... Hold on, they did this once on Newsround Extra, the sun expanding,

50
00:04:59,173 --> 00:05:01,676
- that takes hundreds of years. - Millions.

51
00:05:01,759 --> 00:05:03,803
But the planet's now the property of the National Trust.

52
00:05:03,886 --> 00:05:05,013
They've been keeping it preserved.

53
00:05:05,096 --> 00:05:08,933
See down there? Gravity satellites holding back the sun.

54
00:05:09,767 --> 00:05:11,227
The planet looks the same as ever.

55
00:05:11,311 --> 00:05:13,521
I thought the continent shifted and things.

56
00:05:13,604 --> 00:05:16,733
They did, and the Trust shifted 'em back! That's a classic Earth.

57
00:05:16,816 --> 00:05:19,902
But now the money's run out, nature takes over.

58
00:05:20,945 --> 00:05:22,238
How long's it got?

59
00:05:23,197 --> 00:05:25,700
About half an hour. Then the planet gets roasted.

60
00:05:26,409 --> 00:05:29,996
Is that why we're here? I mean, is that what you do?

61
00:05:30,079 --> 00:05:32,498
Jump in at the last minute and save the Earth?

62
00:05:32,582 --> 00:05:34,917
I'm not saving it. Time's up.

63
00:05:35,418 --> 00:05:39,005
- But what about the people? - It's empty. They've all gone. All left.

64
00:05:43,259 --> 00:05:45,928
- Just me, then. - Who the hell are you?

65
00:05:46,054 --> 00:05:49,057
- Oh, that's nice. Thanks. - But how did you get in?

66
00:05:49,390 --> 00:05:51,851
This is a maximum hospitality zone.

67
00:05:51,934 --> 00:05:54,604
The guests have disembarked! They're on their way any second...

68
00:05:54,729 --> 00:05:57,106
No! That's me. I'm a guest. Look, I've got an invitation.

69
00:05:57,231 --> 00:05:59,275
Look, there you see? It's fine. You see?

70
00:05:59,359 --> 00:06:00,443
"The Doctor, plus one."

71
00:06:00,526 --> 00:06:03,029
I'm the Doctor, this is Rose Tyler, she's my "plus one".

72
00:06:03,112 --> 00:06:04,530
Is that all right?

73
00:06:04,614 --> 00:06:06,449
Well, obviously.

74
00:06:07,784 --> 00:06:09,369
Apologies, et cetera.

75
00:06:09,452 --> 00:06:12,205
If you're on board, we'd better start.

76
00:06:13,414 --> 00:06:15,083
Enjoy.

77
00:06:16,292 --> 00:06:19,629
The paper's slightly psychic. It shows them whatever I want them to see.

78
00:06:19,921 --> 00:06:21,631
Saves a lot of time.

79
00:06:21,756 --> 00:06:23,800
- He's blue. - Yeah.

80
00:06:23,966 --> 00:06:25,051
Okay.

81
00:06:25,134 --> 00:06:28,888
We have in attendance, the Doctor and Rose Tyler!

82
00:06:28,971 --> 00:06:31,808
Thank you. All staff to their positions.

83
00:06:33,643 --> 00:06:36,938
Hurry now! Thank you! Quick as we can, come along, come along!

84
00:06:38,397 --> 00:06:41,150
And now, might I introduce the next honoured guest

85
00:06:41,275 --> 00:06:45,905
representing the Forest of Cheem, we have trees.

86
00:06:46,280 --> 00:06:49,158
Namely Jabe, Lute and Coffa.

87
00:06:49,242 --> 00:06:53,162
There will be an exchange of gifts, representing peace.

88
00:06:53,246 --> 00:06:55,790
If you could keep the room circulating, thank you.

89
00:06:56,165 --> 00:07:02,171
Next, from the solicitors Jolco and Jolco, we have the Moxx of Balhoon.

90
00:07:02,922 --> 00:07:05,675
And next, from Financial Family Seven,

91
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:08,761
we have the Adherents of the Repeated Meme.

92
00:07:09,429 --> 00:07:14,767
The inventors of hyposlip travel systems, the brothers Hop Pyleen! Thank you.

93
00:07:14,851 --> 00:07:16,352
Cal "Sparkplug"...

94
00:07:16,477 --> 00:07:18,020
Mr and Mrs Pakoo.

95
00:07:18,146 --> 00:07:21,190
The ambassadors from the City State of Binding Light...

96
00:07:22,191 --> 00:07:27,029
The gift of peace. I bring you a cutting of my grandfather.

97
00:07:28,614 --> 00:07:32,285
- Thank you. - Yes, gifts, urn...

98
00:07:32,368 --> 00:07:35,955
I give you in return air from my lungs.

99
00:07:39,959 --> 00:07:41,794
How intimate.

100
00:07:41,878 --> 00:07:43,546
There's more where that came from.

101
00:07:44,547 --> 00:07:45,882
I bet there is.

102
00:07:47,884 --> 00:07:51,470
The sponsor of the main event, please welcome...

103
00:07:51,554 --> 00:07:53,222
the Face of Boe.

104
00:07:57,310 --> 00:07:59,312
The Moxx of Balhoon.

105
00:07:59,395 --> 00:08:02,565
My felicitations upon this historical happenstance.

106
00:08:02,732 --> 00:08:04,650
I bring you the gift of bodily salivas.

107
00:08:06,694 --> 00:08:07,987
Thank you very much.

108
00:08:09,822 --> 00:08:12,909
Ah! The Adherents of the Repeated Meme!

109
00:08:12,992 --> 00:08:15,077
I bring you air from my lungs.

110
00:08:18,915 --> 00:08:21,584
A gift of peace. In all good faith.

111
00:08:21,834 --> 00:08:25,588
And last but not least, our very special guest.

112
00:08:25,713 --> 00:08:31,844
Ladies and gentlemen and trees and multiforms, consider the Earth, below.

113
00:08:32,428 --> 00:08:36,724
In memory of this dying world, we call forth...

114
00:08:37,433 --> 00:08:39,602
the last human.

115
00:08:40,520 --> 00:08:44,732
The Lady Cassandra O'Brien Dot Delta Seventeen.

116
00:08:45,441 --> 00:08:49,612
Oh, now don't stare! I know, I know. It's shocking, isn't it?

117
00:08:50,196 --> 00:08:54,784
I've had my chin completely taken away and look at the difference!

118
00:08:54,909 --> 00:08:59,705
Look how thin I am. Thin and dainty!

119
00:09:00,081 --> 00:09:02,291
I don't look a day over 2,000.

120
00:09:03,459 --> 00:09:05,753
Moisturise me, moisturise me!

121
00:09:06,963 --> 00:09:09,924
Truly, I am the last human.

122
00:09:10,466 --> 00:09:15,054
My father was a Texan, my mother was from the Arctic desert.

123
00:09:16,055 --> 00:09:18,641
They were born on the Earth

124
00:09:18,766 --> 00:09:22,436
and they were the last to be buried in its soil.

125
00:09:23,479 --> 00:09:28,818
I have come to honour them and say goodbye.

126
00:09:30,152 --> 00:09:32,780
Oh, no tears, no tears...

127
00:09:33,489 --> 00:09:34,907
I'm sorry.

128
00:09:37,076 --> 00:09:40,496
But behold! I bring gifts!

129
00:09:40,955 --> 00:09:45,793
From Earth itself, the last remaining ostrich egg.

130
00:09:46,586 --> 00:09:50,172
Legend says, it had a wingspan of 50 feet!

131
00:09:50,256 --> 00:09:52,592
And blew fire from its nostrils.

132
00:09:53,092 --> 00:09:54,760
Or was that my third husband?

133
00:09:54,844 --> 00:09:59,098
Oh, no, oh, don't laugh, I'll get laughter-lines.

134
00:09:59,181 --> 00:10:01,267
No, stop!

135
00:10:03,019 --> 00:10:04,937
Mercy!

136
00:10:05,354 --> 00:10:08,357
And here! Another rarity.

137
00:10:09,150 --> 00:10:13,029
According to the archives, this was called an iPod.

138
00:10:13,154 --> 00:10:17,366
It stores classical music from humanity's greatest composers.

139
00:10:17,658 --> 00:10:18,909
Play on!

140
00:10:29,295 --> 00:10:31,464
The refreshments will now be served.

141
00:10:32,381 --> 00:10:34,467
Earth-death in 30 minutes.

142
00:10:34,550 --> 00:10:40,222
♪ Sometimes I feel I've got to run away

143
00:10:40,306 --> 00:10:44,894
♪ I've got to get away from the pain

144
00:10:44,977 --> 00:10:48,481
♪ That you drive into the heart of me

145
00:10:48,564 --> 00:10:54,904
♪ The love we share seems to go nowhere

146
00:10:55,029 --> 00:10:58,491
♪ And I've lost my light

147
00:10:58,574 --> 00:11:02,495
♪ For I toss and turn I can't sleep at night... ♪

148
00:11:02,578 --> 00:11:05,247
- Doctor.

149
00:11:05,331 --> 00:11:06,749
Thank you.

150
00:11:08,417 --> 00:11:11,337
A gift of peace in all good faith.

151
00:11:11,420 --> 00:11:14,340
No, you're very kind, but I'm just the steward.

152
00:11:14,423 --> 00:11:18,094
A gift of peace in all good faith.

153
00:11:18,219 --> 00:11:21,430
Oh, yes. Thank you. Of course.

154
00:11:21,889 --> 00:11:23,432
Identify species.

155
00:11:25,935 --> 00:11:28,062
Please identify species.

156
00:11:28,396 --> 00:11:29,939
Now stop it!

157
00:11:30,022 --> 00:11:32,775
Identify his race. Where's he from?

158
00:11:36,529 --> 00:11:38,239
It's impossible.

159
00:12:08,269 --> 00:12:11,063
Sorry, am I allowed to be in here?

160
00:12:11,814 --> 00:12:14,608
You have to give us permission to talk.

161
00:12:16,318 --> 00:12:17,987
Urn...

162
00:12:19,488 --> 00:12:23,325
- You have permission. - Thank you.

163
00:12:24,118 --> 00:12:26,620
And, no, you're not in the way.

164
00:12:26,704 --> 00:12:29,373
- Guests are allowed anywhere. - Okay.

165
00:12:34,170 --> 00:12:36,839
- What's your name? - Raffalo.

166
00:12:37,339 --> 00:12:39,717
- Raffalo? - Yes, miss.

167
00:12:40,926 --> 00:12:44,180
I won't be long, I've just got to carry out some maintenance.

168
00:12:46,015 --> 00:12:48,434
There's a tiny little glitch in the Face of Boe's suite.

169
00:12:48,726 --> 00:12:50,978
There must be something blocking the system.

170
00:12:51,061 --> 00:12:53,439
He's not getting any hot water.

171
00:12:54,273 --> 00:12:57,526
- So, you're a plumber? - That's right, miss.

172
00:12:58,944 --> 00:13:00,946
They still have plumbers?

173
00:13:01,030 --> 00:13:02,948
I hope so, else I'm out of a job!

174
00:13:04,325 --> 00:13:07,244
- Where are you from? - Crespallion.

175
00:13:09,121 --> 00:13:11,415
That's a planet, is it?

176
00:13:11,790 --> 00:13:14,710
No, Crespallion's part of the Jaggit Brocade,

177
00:13:14,794 --> 00:13:17,838
affiliated to the Scarlet Junction, Convex 56.

178
00:13:18,047 --> 00:13:21,300
And where are you from, miss? If you don't mind me asking.

179
00:13:21,425 --> 00:13:23,594
No, not at all. Um...

180
00:13:24,929 --> 00:13:28,057
I don't know. A long way away.

181
00:13:29,642 --> 00:13:32,811
I just sort of hitched a lift with this man...

182
00:13:34,271 --> 00:13:38,818
I didn't even think about it. Don't even know who he is.

183
00:13:41,362 --> 00:13:43,447
He's a complete stranger.

184
00:13:45,157 --> 00:13:48,702
Anyway, don't let me keep you. Good luck with it!

185
00:13:49,119 --> 00:13:54,124
Thank you, miss. And thank you for the permission.

186
00:13:54,208 --> 00:13:56,377
Not many people are that considerate.

187
00:13:56,460 --> 00:13:58,295
Okay. See you later.

188
00:14:06,720 --> 00:14:08,138
Now, then.

189
00:14:08,222 --> 00:14:11,892
Control, I'm at junction 19. I think the problem's coming from in here.

190
00:14:11,976 --> 00:14:13,894
I'll go inside and have a look.

191
00:14:15,187 --> 00:14:18,315
What's that? Something in there?

192
00:14:19,066 --> 00:14:20,985
Ooh. Who are you, then?

193
00:14:21,402 --> 00:14:22,570
Hold on!

194
00:14:24,238 --> 00:14:27,575
If you're an upgrade, I just need to register you, that's all.

195
00:14:27,658 --> 00:14:29,118
Oh, come back.

196
00:14:30,327 --> 00:14:32,705
Ah, there you are.

197
00:14:33,122 --> 00:14:35,541
Now, I just need to register your ident.

198
00:14:36,917 --> 00:14:41,255
Aw, there's two of ya! Got yourself a little mate?

199
00:14:43,465 --> 00:14:46,260
I think I'd better report this to control.

200
00:14:46,343 --> 00:14:48,721
How many of you are there?

201
00:14:50,097 --> 00:14:51,515
What are you?

202
00:14:52,433 --> 00:14:55,185
Oh, no! No!

203
00:15:07,364 --> 00:15:09,325
- What's that?

204
00:15:09,408 --> 00:15:11,785
- Well, how should I know?

205
00:15:14,288 --> 00:15:18,542
Would the owner of the blue box in private gallery 15

206
00:15:18,626 --> 00:15:21,086
please report to the steward's office immediately.

207
00:15:22,546 --> 00:15:26,592
Guests are reminded that the use of teleportation devices

208
00:15:26,675 --> 00:15:32,222
is strictly prohibited under Peace Treaty 5.4/Cup/16. Thank you.

209
00:15:32,431 --> 00:15:35,976
Earth-death in 25 minutes.

210
00:15:36,060 --> 00:15:39,063
Earth-death in 25 minutes.

211
00:15:39,146 --> 00:15:41,231
Oh, thanks.

212
00:15:47,738 --> 00:15:48,989
Hello!

213
00:15:49,406 --> 00:15:52,868
My name's Rose. That's a sort of plant.

214
00:15:54,078 --> 00:15:55,913
We might be related.

215
00:15:57,873 --> 00:15:59,833
I'm talking to a twig.

216
00:16:11,261 --> 00:16:14,973
Oi, now, careful with that, park it properly. No scratches.

217
00:16:38,247 --> 00:16:40,582
Rose, are you in there?

218
00:16:42,876 --> 00:16:44,211
Aye-aye!

219
00:16:46,588 --> 00:16:49,883
- What d'you think, then? - Great, yeah. Fine.

220
00:16:49,967 --> 00:16:52,886
Once you get past the slightly psychic paper.

221
00:16:55,639 --> 00:16:57,766
They're just so alien!

222
00:16:59,852 --> 00:17:02,396
The aliens are so alien.

223
00:17:04,231 --> 00:17:07,192
You look at 'em, and they're alien.

224
00:17:07,401 --> 00:17:09,778
Good thing I didn't take you to the deep south.

225
00:17:12,364 --> 00:17:15,492
- Where are you from? - All over the place.

226
00:17:16,785 --> 00:17:19,455
- They all speak English. - No, you just hear English.

227
00:17:19,538 --> 00:17:21,790
It's a gift of the Tardis. It's the telepathic field,

228
00:17:21,874 --> 00:17:24,001
gets inside your brain, translates.

229
00:17:24,084 --> 00:17:27,045
- It's inside my brain? - Well, in a good way.

230
00:17:27,671 --> 00:17:29,798
Your machine gets inside my head?

231
00:17:29,882 --> 00:17:33,343
It gets inside and it changes my mind and you didn't even ask.

232
00:17:33,802 --> 00:17:35,387
I didn't think about it like that.

233
00:17:35,471 --> 00:17:38,891
No, you were too busy thinking up cheap shots about the deep south!

234
00:17:40,017 --> 00:17:42,102
Who are you then, Doctor.

235
00:17:42,895 --> 00:17:45,063
What're you called? What sort of alien are you?

236
00:17:45,147 --> 00:17:47,649
- I'm just a Doctor. - From what planet?

237
00:17:47,733 --> 00:17:49,526
Well, it's not as if you'd know where it is.

238
00:17:49,610 --> 00:17:51,528
- Where're you from? - What does it matter?

239
00:17:51,612 --> 00:17:53,447
- Tell me who you are! - This is who I am.

240
00:17:53,530 --> 00:17:55,073
Right here, right now. All right?

241
00:17:55,157 --> 00:17:57,910
All that counts is here and now, and this is me!

242
00:17:57,993 --> 00:18:02,289
Yeah, and I'm here too 'cause you brought me here! So just tell me!

243
00:18:10,756 --> 00:18:13,926
Earth-death in 20 minutes.

244
00:18:15,385 --> 00:18:18,806
Earth-death in 20 minutes.

245
00:18:26,396 --> 00:18:27,856
All right.

246
00:18:29,525 --> 00:18:32,069
As my mate Shireen says,

247
00:18:32,152 --> 00:18:35,030
"Don't argue with the designated driver."

248
00:18:37,199 --> 00:18:39,118
Can't exactly call for a taxi.

249
00:18:40,327 --> 00:18:41,870
There's no signal.

250
00:18:42,871 --> 00:18:45,707
We're out of range. Just a bit.

251
00:18:47,876 --> 00:18:51,171
Tell you what, with a little bit of jiggery-pokery...

252
00:18:51,255 --> 00:18:53,507
Is that a technical term, "jiggery-pokery"?

253
00:18:53,590 --> 00:18:55,884
Yeah, I came first in jiggery-pokery. What about you?

254
00:18:55,968 --> 00:18:58,512
- No, I failed hullabaloo. - Aw.

255
00:19:01,390 --> 00:19:02,766
There you go.

256
00:19:15,404 --> 00:19:17,030
- Hello? - Mum?

257
00:19:17,114 --> 00:19:20,492
Oh, what is it? What's wrong? What have I done now?

258
00:19:20,576 --> 00:19:24,163
Ooh, this red top's falling to bits! You should get your money back.

259
00:19:24,246 --> 00:19:26,123
Go on, there must be something.

260
00:19:26,206 --> 00:19:27,916
You never phone in the middle of the day.

261
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:30,294
- What's so funny?

262
00:19:30,377 --> 00:19:32,421
Nothing. You all right, though?

263
00:19:32,504 --> 00:19:34,089
Yeah, why wouldn't I be?

264
00:19:34,673 --> 00:19:39,344
- What day is it? - Wednesday all day. You got a hangover?

265
00:19:39,428 --> 00:19:42,055
Oh, I tell you what, put a quid in that lottery syndicate.

266
00:19:42,139 --> 00:19:43,557
I'll pay you back later.

267
00:19:43,640 --> 00:19:48,353
Yeah, um, I was just calling 'cause I might be late home.

268
00:19:48,729 --> 00:19:49,938
Is there something wrong?

269
00:19:50,230 --> 00:19:54,151
No, I'm fine. Top of the world!

270
00:19:59,156 --> 00:20:02,701
If you think that's amazing, you wanna see the bill.

271
00:20:02,784 --> 00:20:05,204
That was five billion years ago.

272
00:20:06,205 --> 00:20:07,623
So...

273
00:20:07,706 --> 00:20:09,249
She's dead now.

274
00:20:11,460 --> 00:20:14,463
Five billion years later, my mum's dead.

275
00:20:14,588 --> 00:20:16,381
Bundle of laughs, you are.

276
00:20:21,678 --> 00:20:23,764
That's not supposed to happen.

277
00:20:23,847 --> 00:20:27,601
Well, what was it? I'm just getting green lights at this end.

278
00:20:27,684 --> 00:20:29,978
Honoured guests may be reassured

279
00:20:30,062 --> 00:20:34,483
that gravity pockets may cause slight turbulence. Thanking you.

280
00:20:34,566 --> 00:20:37,444
The whole place shook! I felt it!

281
00:20:37,527 --> 00:20:41,240
I've hosted all sorts of events on platforms one, three, six and fifteen

282
00:20:41,323 --> 00:20:43,533
and I've never felt the slightest tremor!

283
00:20:43,617 --> 00:20:46,495
I warn you, if this lot decide to sue...

284
00:20:46,578 --> 00:20:48,372
I'm gonna scan the infrastructure.

285
00:20:53,794 --> 00:20:55,462
What's that?

286
00:20:56,546 --> 00:20:59,466
Control, I don't want to worry you, but I'm picking up readings...

287
00:21:01,093 --> 00:21:05,806
I have no idea! They're small. The scan says they're metal...

288
00:21:05,889 --> 00:21:08,392
I don't know what they look like!

289
00:21:11,270 --> 00:21:15,065
Although I imagine they might look rather like that.

290
00:21:18,360 --> 00:21:22,864
You're not on the guest list. How did you get on board?

291
00:21:27,911 --> 00:21:30,872
- No! No! - Sunfilter deactivated.

292
00:21:31,123 --> 00:21:33,166
Sunfilter descending.

293
00:21:33,333 --> 00:21:34,584
Sunfilter up! No, no, no!

294
00:21:34,710 --> 00:21:37,421
External temperature 430 degrees.

295
00:21:37,546 --> 00:21:39,339
- Control! Respond! - Sunfilter descending.

296
00:21:39,423 --> 00:21:41,758
- Sunfilter up! - Sunfilter descending.

297
00:22:08,243 --> 00:22:12,289
That wasn't a gravity pocket. I know gravity pockets, and they don't feel like that.

298
00:22:12,748 --> 00:22:14,374
What do you think, Jabe?

299
00:22:14,458 --> 00:22:16,710
Listen to the engines, they're pitched up about 30 Hertz.

300
00:22:16,752 --> 00:22:18,337
Is that dodgy or what?

301
00:22:18,420 --> 00:22:21,089
It's the sound of metal, that doesn't make any sense to me.

302
00:22:21,840 --> 00:22:24,843
- Where's the engine room? - I don't know.

303
00:22:25,177 --> 00:22:28,722
But the maintenance duct is just behind our guests' suite, I could show you.

304
00:22:28,805 --> 00:22:31,141
And your wife.

305
00:22:31,266 --> 00:22:32,726
Oh, she's not my wife.

306
00:22:32,809 --> 00:22:34,478
- Partner? - No.

307
00:22:34,603 --> 00:22:36,938
- Concubine? - Nope.

308
00:22:37,022 --> 00:22:38,106
Prostitute?

309
00:22:39,358 --> 00:22:42,152
Whatever I am, it must be invisible! Do you mind?

310
00:22:42,778 --> 00:22:44,988
Tell you what, you two go and pollinate.

311
00:22:45,113 --> 00:22:46,907
I'm gonna catch up with the Family.

312
00:22:46,990 --> 00:22:48,867
Quick word with Michael Jackson.

313
00:22:49,451 --> 00:22:51,244
Don't start a fight.

314
00:22:51,328 --> 00:22:53,038
I'm all yours.

315
00:22:55,874 --> 00:22:57,501
And I want you home by midnight!

316
00:22:59,044 --> 00:23:04,341
Earth-death in 15 minutes. Earth-death in 75 minutes.

317
00:23:14,476 --> 00:23:17,854
Who's in charge of Platform One? Has it got a captain or what?

318
00:23:17,979 --> 00:23:20,232
There's just the steward and the staff.

319
00:23:20,315 --> 00:23:22,859
All the rest is controlled by the metal mind.

320
00:23:22,984 --> 00:23:25,445
You mean, the computer? Well, who controls that?

321
00:23:25,529 --> 00:23:26,988
The Corporation.

322
00:23:27,072 --> 00:23:30,867
They move Platform One from one artistic event to another.

323
00:23:31,493 --> 00:23:33,578
Well, there's no one from the Corporation on board.

324
00:23:33,662 --> 00:23:37,541
They're not needed. This facility is purely automatic.

325
00:23:37,666 --> 00:23:39,376
It's the height of the Alpha Class.

326
00:23:39,501 --> 00:23:41,962
- Nothing can go wrong. - Unsinkable?

327
00:23:42,045 --> 00:23:45,298
If you like. The nautical metaphor is appropriate.

328
00:23:45,382 --> 00:23:47,509
You're telling me! I was on board another ship once.

329
00:23:47,634 --> 00:23:49,052
They said that was unsinkable.

330
00:23:49,177 --> 00:23:52,722
I ended up clinging to an iceberg. It wasn't half cold.

331
00:23:52,848 --> 00:23:57,978
So, what you're saying is, if we get in trouble, there's no one to help us out?

332
00:23:58,061 --> 00:24:00,564
- I'm afraid not. - Fantastic!

333
00:24:01,565 --> 00:24:05,360
I don't understand. In what way is that fantastic?

334
00:24:11,074 --> 00:24:14,995
Soon the sun will blossom into a red giant,

335
00:24:15,078 --> 00:24:17,038
and my home will die.

336
00:24:17,164 --> 00:24:20,709
That's where I used to live, when I was a little boy. Down there.

337
00:24:20,834 --> 00:24:24,880
Mummy and Daddy had a house built into the side of the Los Angeles Crevasse.

338
00:24:25,005 --> 00:24:27,340
I'd have such fun.

339
00:24:27,757 --> 00:24:29,509
What happened to everyone else?

340
00:24:29,593 --> 00:24:31,720
The human race, where did it go?

341
00:24:32,596 --> 00:24:36,475
They say mankind has touched every star in the sky.

342
00:24:36,558 --> 00:24:38,393
So you're not the last human.

343
00:24:39,019 --> 00:24:42,230
I am the last pure human.

344
00:24:43,023 --> 00:24:45,275
The others mingled.

345
00:24:45,775 --> 00:24:48,570
Oh, they call themselves New-humans and Proto-humans

346
00:24:48,695 --> 00:24:50,739
and Digi-humans, even Human-ish!

347
00:24:50,864 --> 00:24:53,366
But do you know what I call them?

348
00:24:53,450 --> 00:24:54,784
Mongrels.

349
00:24:55,535 --> 00:24:58,079
Right. And you stayed behind.

350
00:24:58,538 --> 00:25:01,041
- I kept myself pure. - Hmm.

351
00:25:01,583 --> 00:25:03,710
How many operations have you had?

352
00:25:04,044 --> 00:25:09,049
708. Next week, it's 709. I'm having my blood bleached.

353
00:25:10,592 --> 00:25:12,469
Is that why you wanted a word?

354
00:25:12,886 --> 00:25:15,055
You could be flatter, Rose.

355
00:25:15,138 --> 00:25:18,266
You've got a little bit of a chin poking out.

356
00:25:18,391 --> 00:25:21,728
- I'd rather die. - Honestly, it doesn't hurt.

357
00:25:22,229 --> 00:25:24,356
I mean it. I would rather die.

358
00:25:24,439 --> 00:25:28,652
It's better to die than to live like you, a bitchy trampoline.

359
00:25:28,777 --> 00:25:31,279
Oh, well, what do you know?

360
00:25:32,113 --> 00:25:34,199
I was born on that planet!

361
00:25:34,282 --> 00:25:36,701
And so was my mum and so was my dad.

362
00:25:36,785 --> 00:25:39,788
And that makes me, officially, the last human being in this room.

363
00:25:39,913 --> 00:25:41,790
'Cause you're not human.

364
00:25:41,957 --> 00:25:46,002
You've had it all nipped and tucked and ﬂattened till there's nothing left.

365
00:25:46,127 --> 00:25:47,921
Anything human got chucked in the bin!

366
00:25:48,004 --> 00:25:51,341
You're just skin, Cassandra! Lipstick and skin.

367
00:25:52,133 --> 00:25:53,635
Nice talking.

368
00:26:01,643 --> 00:26:06,564
So, tell me, Jabe, what's a tree like you doing in a place like this?

369
00:26:06,648 --> 00:26:08,733
- Respect for the Earth. - Come on!

370
00:26:08,817 --> 00:26:11,152
Everyone on this platform is worth zillions!

371
00:26:11,236 --> 00:26:15,740
Well, perhaps it's a case of having to be seen at the right occasions.

372
00:26:15,824 --> 00:26:17,659
In case your share prices drop?

373
00:26:17,742 --> 00:26:21,329
I know you lot. You've got massive forests everywhere, roots everywhere!

374
00:26:21,413 --> 00:26:23,498
And there's always money in land.

375
00:26:23,623 --> 00:26:25,250
All the same.

376
00:26:25,333 --> 00:26:27,919
We respect the Earth as family.

377
00:26:28,003 --> 00:26:31,923
So many species evolved from that planet. Mankind is only one.

378
00:26:32,007 --> 00:26:33,425
I am another.

379
00:26:33,508 --> 00:26:37,012
My ancestors were transplanted from the planet down below.

380
00:26:37,095 --> 00:26:40,265
And I'm a direct descendant of the tropical rainforest.

381
00:26:40,348 --> 00:26:42,183
Excuse me.

382
00:26:44,936 --> 00:26:47,147
And what about your ancestry, Doctor?

383
00:26:49,024 --> 00:26:51,818
Perhaps you could tell a story or two.

384
00:26:53,528 --> 00:26:58,700
Perhaps a man only enjoys trouble when there's nothing else left?

385
00:27:00,535 --> 00:27:02,537
I scanned you earlier.

386
00:27:03,955 --> 00:27:06,958
The metal machine had trouble identifying your species.

387
00:27:07,042 --> 00:27:08,877
It refused to admit your existence.

388
00:27:09,294 --> 00:27:12,630
And even when it named you, I wouldn't believe it.

389
00:27:12,964 --> 00:27:14,674
But it was right.

390
00:27:15,884 --> 00:27:18,136
I know where you're from!

391
00:27:20,347 --> 00:27:24,392
Forgive me for intruding, but it's remarkable that you even exist!

392
00:27:26,019 --> 00:27:28,063
I just want to say...

393
00:27:29,356 --> 00:27:31,399
how sorry I am.

394
00:28:02,847 --> 00:28:05,225
Is it me, or is it a bit nippy?

395
00:28:28,415 --> 00:28:30,792
Fair dos, though, that's a great bit of air-conditioning.

396
00:28:30,875 --> 00:28:32,544
Sort of nice and old fashioned.

397
00:28:32,627 --> 00:28:34,129
Bet they call it retro.

398
00:28:36,089 --> 00:28:37,632
Gotcha!

399
00:28:43,805 --> 00:28:47,475
- What the hell is that? - Is it part of the "retro"?

400
00:28:47,600 --> 00:28:49,811
I don't think so, hold on.

401
00:28:57,152 --> 00:29:00,488
- Hey, nice Liana! - Thank you.

402
00:29:00,572 --> 00:29:02,240
Not supposed to show them in public.

403
00:29:02,323 --> 00:29:04,659
Don't worry, I won't tell anybody.

404
00:29:04,743 --> 00:29:07,537
Now, then, who's been bringing their pets on board?

405
00:29:07,620 --> 00:29:09,747
- What does it do? - Sabotage...

406
00:29:09,831 --> 00:29:12,250
Earth-death in 10 minutes...

407
00:29:12,333 --> 00:29:15,003
And the temperature's about to rocket. Come on.

408
00:29:16,963 --> 00:29:19,382
The planet's end!

409
00:29:19,466 --> 00:29:21,926
Come gather, come gather!

410
00:29:22,010 --> 00:29:25,638
Bid farewell to the cradle of civilisation.

411
00:29:25,722 --> 00:29:29,392
Let us mourn her with a traditional ballad.

412
00:29:36,357 --> 00:29:39,944
♪ Baby, can't you see? I'm calling

413
00:29:40,028 --> 00:29:43,448
♪ A guy like you should wear a warning

414
00:29:43,531 --> 00:29:46,576
♪ It's dangerous I'm fallin'... ♪

415
00:29:46,659 --> 00:29:48,536
All right, hold on, get back!

416
00:29:51,790 --> 00:29:55,710
Sunfilter rising. Sunfilter rising.

417
00:29:55,793 --> 00:29:58,004
- Is the steward in there? - You can smell him.

418
00:29:59,339 --> 00:30:02,342
Hold on. There's another sunfilter programmed to descend.

419
00:30:04,302 --> 00:30:07,514
♪ Too high can't come down

420
00:30:07,597 --> 00:30:12,936
♪ Losing my head Spinning round and round

421
00:30:13,019 --> 00:30:14,938
♪ Do you feel me now? ♪

422
00:30:15,021 --> 00:30:20,109
Sunfilter descending. Sunfilter descending.

423
00:30:25,615 --> 00:30:27,867
Sunfilter descending.

424
00:30:27,951 --> 00:30:30,829
- Let me out! Let me out! - Sunfilter descending.

425
00:30:33,623 --> 00:30:36,000
Let me out! Let me out! Let me out!

426
00:30:36,084 --> 00:30:41,005
Sunfilter descending. Sunfilter descending.

427
00:30:41,089 --> 00:30:42,799
Anyone in there?

428
00:30:42,882 --> 00:30:45,927
- Let me out! - Oh, well, it would be you.

429
00:30:46,010 --> 00:30:48,972
- Open the door! - Hold on, give us two ticks.

430
00:30:49,180 --> 00:30:54,394
Sunfilter descending. Sunfilter descending.

431
00:30:55,853 --> 00:30:59,774
Sunfilter rising. Sunfilter rising.

432
00:31:01,442 --> 00:31:06,114
Sunfilter rising. Sunfilter rising...

433
00:31:06,197 --> 00:31:08,283
Sunfilter descending.

434
00:31:08,867 --> 00:31:11,452
It's just what I need. The computer's getting clever.

435
00:31:11,536 --> 00:31:15,456
- Stop mucking about! - I'm not mucking about! It's fighting back.

436
00:31:15,582 --> 00:31:17,250
- Sunfilter descending. - Open the door!

437
00:31:17,292 --> 00:31:18,334
I know!

438
00:31:18,418 --> 00:31:22,255
- Sunfilter descending. - The lock's melted!

439
00:31:23,798 --> 00:31:28,761
Sunfilter descending. Sunfilter descending.

440
00:31:32,390 --> 00:31:36,144
Sunfilter rising. Sunfilter rising.

441
00:31:42,817 --> 00:31:46,321
The opening's jammed! I can't open the door. Stay there, don't move!

442
00:31:46,404 --> 00:31:48,323
Where am I gonna go? Ipswich?

443
00:31:48,531 --> 00:31:50,992
Earth-death in five minutes.

444
00:31:53,286 --> 00:31:55,705
The metal machine confirms...

445
00:31:55,788 --> 00:31:58,833
the spider devices have infiltrated the whole of Platform One.

446
00:32:00,251 --> 00:32:03,421
How's that possible? Our private rooms are protected by a code-wall.

447
00:32:03,504 --> 00:32:05,715
Moisturise me, moisturise me.

448
00:32:05,840 --> 00:32:07,717
Summon the steward!

449
00:32:07,800 --> 00:32:09,552
I'm afraid the steward is dead.

450
00:32:14,307 --> 00:32:15,850
Who killed him?

451
00:32:15,934 --> 00:32:19,479
This whole event was sponsored by the Face of Boe! He invited us.

452
00:32:19,562 --> 00:32:21,481
Talk to the face! Talk to the face!

453
00:32:21,564 --> 00:32:24,651
Easy way of finding out. Someone brought their little pet on board.

454
00:32:25,151 --> 00:32:26,527
Let's send him back to master.

455
00:32:49,050 --> 00:32:52,261
The Adherents of the Repeated Meme!

456
00:32:52,387 --> 00:32:55,014
That's all very well and really kinda obvious.

457
00:32:55,098 --> 00:32:57,225
But if you stop and think about it...

458
00:32:59,018 --> 00:33:01,270
A Repeated Meme is just an idea.

459
00:33:01,521 --> 00:33:03,815
And that's all they are, an idea.

460
00:33:07,819 --> 00:33:11,823
Remote-control droids. Nice little cover for the real troublemaker.

461
00:33:12,281 --> 00:33:14,409
Go on, Jimbo. Go home.

462
00:33:18,579 --> 00:33:21,666
I bet you were the school swot and never got kissed.

463
00:33:21,874 --> 00:33:23,209
At arms!

464
00:33:23,418 --> 00:33:25,003
What you gonna do, moisturise me?

465
00:33:25,128 --> 00:33:26,462
With acid.

466
00:33:26,546 --> 00:33:28,297
Oh, you're too late anyway.

467
00:33:28,840 --> 00:33:31,509
My spiders have control of the main frame.

468
00:33:31,634 --> 00:33:36,639
Oh, you all carried them as gifts, tax-free, past every code-wall.

469
00:33:37,974 --> 00:33:39,767
I'm not just a pretty face.

470
00:33:39,851 --> 00:33:42,770
Sabotaging a ship while you're still inside it, how stupid is that?

471
00:33:42,937 --> 00:33:45,898
I'd hoped to manufacture a hostage situation.

472
00:33:45,982 --> 00:33:48,025
With myself as one of the victims.

473
00:33:48,818 --> 00:33:51,654
The compensation would've been enormous.

474
00:33:51,779 --> 00:33:54,407
Five billion years, and it still comes down to money.

475
00:33:54,824 --> 00:33:57,410
Do you think it's cheap, looking like this?

476
00:33:57,493 --> 00:33:59,996
Flatness costs a fortune!

477
00:34:01,164 --> 00:34:02,915
I am the last human, Doctor.

478
00:34:03,750 --> 00:34:07,712
Me, not that freaky little kid of yours.

479
00:34:07,879 --> 00:34:10,173
Arrest her! The infidel!

480
00:34:10,256 --> 00:34:14,552
Oh, shut it, pixie! I've still got my final option.

481
00:34:14,635 --> 00:34:16,888
Earth-death in three minutes.

482
00:34:16,971 --> 00:34:21,267
And here it comes. You're just as useful dead, all of you.

483
00:34:21,851 --> 00:34:24,145
I have shares in your rival companies.

484
00:34:24,228 --> 00:34:26,439
And they'll triple in price as soon as your dead.

485
00:34:27,106 --> 00:34:30,610
My spiders are primed and ready to destroy the safety systems.

486
00:34:30,943 --> 00:34:33,613
How did that old Earth song go?

487
00:34:33,696 --> 00:34:35,198
"Burn baby, burn."

488
00:34:35,281 --> 00:34:36,866
Then you'll burn with us!

489
00:34:36,949 --> 00:34:39,118
Oh, I'm so sorry!

490
00:34:39,452 --> 00:34:44,207
I know the use of teleportation is strictly forbidden, but...

491
00:34:44,290 --> 00:34:46,125
I'm such a naughty thing.

492
00:34:46,793 --> 00:34:48,753
Spiders, activate!

493
00:34:58,387 --> 00:35:02,642
Force-fields gone, with the planet about to explode...

494
00:35:02,725 --> 00:35:04,352
At least it'll be quick.

495
00:35:04,727 --> 00:35:07,271
Just like my fifth husband...

496
00:35:07,355 --> 00:35:11,234
Oh, shame on me! Bye-bye, darlings.

497
00:35:11,317 --> 00:35:14,111
- Safety systems failing. - Bye-bye, my darlings!

498
00:35:14,737 --> 00:35:17,156
Heat levels rising.

499
00:35:17,240 --> 00:35:19,951
- Reset the computer! - Only the steward would know how.

500
00:35:20,034 --> 00:35:21,869
No, we can do it by hand.

501
00:35:21,953 --> 00:35:24,956
There must be a system restore switch. Jabe, come on!

502
00:35:25,039 --> 00:35:26,541
You lot, just chill.

503
00:35:26,666 --> 00:35:27,667
Heat levels rising.

504
00:35:32,338 --> 00:35:37,134
Earth-death in two minutes. Earth-death in two minutes.

505
00:35:39,011 --> 00:35:44,433
Heat levels critical. Heat levels critical.

506
00:35:47,645 --> 00:35:50,064
Oh, and guess where the switch is.

507
00:35:51,065 --> 00:35:55,027
Heat levels rising. Heat levels rising.

508
00:36:04,954 --> 00:36:09,292
External temperature 5,000 degrees.

509
00:36:18,968 --> 00:36:21,888
You can't, the heat's gonna vent through this place.

510
00:36:21,971 --> 00:36:24,182
- I know. - Jabe, you're made of wood.

511
00:36:24,265 --> 00:36:27,435
Then stop wasting time, Time Lord.

512
00:36:30,730 --> 00:36:34,817
Heat levels rising. Heat levels rising.

513
00:36:36,444 --> 00:36:38,779
Heat levels hazardous.

514
00:36:38,863 --> 00:36:42,533
- We're going to die! - Heat levels hazardous.

515
00:36:57,214 --> 00:36:59,800
Shields malfunction.

516
00:37:01,010 --> 00:37:03,429
Shields malfunction.

517
00:37:04,805 --> 00:37:08,309
Shields malfunction.

518
00:37:08,392 --> 00:37:11,229
Shields malfunction.

519
00:37:16,817 --> 00:37:22,615
Heat levels critical. Heat levels critical.

520
00:37:35,336 --> 00:37:40,049
Heat levels rising. Heat levels rising.

521
00:38:07,618 --> 00:38:09,620
Planet explodes in...

522
00:38:10,538 --> 00:38:12,206
ten,

523
00:38:12,832 --> 00:38:14,417
nine,

524
00:38:16,043 --> 00:38:17,753
eight,

525
00:38:19,880 --> 00:38:21,424
seven,

526
00:38:23,301 --> 00:38:24,802
six,

527
00:38:27,179 --> 00:38:28,639
five,

528
00:38:30,433 --> 00:38:31,934
four...

529
00:38:35,521 --> 00:38:36,814
Raise shields!

530
00:38:37,773 --> 00:38:39,025
One.

531
00:38:55,541 --> 00:39:00,004
Exoglass repair. Exoglass repair.

532
00:39:04,175 --> 00:39:08,846
Exoglass repair. Exoglass repair.

533
00:39:55,017 --> 00:39:57,061
- You all right? - Yeah, I'm fine.

534
00:39:57,144 --> 00:39:59,563
I'm full of ideas. I'm bristling with 'em!

535
00:39:59,647 --> 00:40:03,109
Idea number one, teleportation through 5,000 degrees

536
00:40:03,192 --> 00:40:05,027
needs some kind of feed.

537
00:40:05,111 --> 00:40:08,697
Idea number two. This feed must be hidden nearby.

538
00:40:12,451 --> 00:40:13,619
Idea number three.

539
00:40:13,702 --> 00:40:18,082
If you're as clever as me, then a teleportation-feed can be reversed.

540
00:40:19,542 --> 00:40:24,171
Oh, you should've seen their little alien faces...

541
00:40:26,382 --> 00:40:28,759
- Oh. - The last human.

542
00:40:28,843 --> 00:40:31,887
So, you passed my little test. Bravo!

543
00:40:31,971 --> 00:40:35,141
This makes you eligible to join the... the Human Club.

544
00:40:35,224 --> 00:40:38,060
People have died Cassandra, you murdered them.

545
00:40:38,144 --> 00:40:40,312
It depends on your definition of people!

546
00:40:40,396 --> 00:40:44,275
And that's enough of a technicality to keep your lawyers dizzy for centuries!

547
00:40:44,358 --> 00:40:49,321
Take me to court then, Doctor, and watch me smile and cry...

548
00:40:51,031 --> 00:40:52,783
- ...and ﬂutter. - And creak?

549
00:40:53,325 --> 00:40:56,036
- And what? - Creak! You're creaking.

550
00:40:56,996 --> 00:40:59,039
What?

551
00:40:59,123 --> 00:41:01,041
I'm drying out!

552
00:41:01,292 --> 00:41:05,045
Oh, sweet heavens! Moisturise me, moisturise me!

553
00:41:05,129 --> 00:41:08,090
Where are my surgeons? My lovely boys!

554
00:41:08,174 --> 00:41:11,051
- It's too hot! - You raised the temperature.

555
00:41:11,218 --> 00:41:13,429
Have pity!

556
00:41:13,512 --> 00:41:15,222
Moisturise me!

557
00:41:15,306 --> 00:41:17,600
Oh, Doctor!

558
00:41:17,683 --> 00:41:19,185
Help her.

559
00:41:19,268 --> 00:41:21,812
Everything has its time and everything dies.

560
00:41:22,646 --> 00:41:26,942
I'm too young!

561
00:41:39,788 --> 00:41:42,708
Shuttles four and six departing.

562
00:41:43,125 --> 00:41:46,629
This unit now closing dawn for maintenance.

563
00:42:02,061 --> 00:42:03,979
The end of the Earth.

564
00:42:05,814 --> 00:42:07,483
It's gone.

565
00:42:10,402 --> 00:42:13,906
We were too busy saving ourselves. No one saw it go.

566
00:42:18,535 --> 00:42:22,581
All those years, all that history, and no one was even looking!

567
00:42:24,583 --> 00:42:26,585
It's just...

568
00:42:27,795 --> 00:42:29,129
Come with me.

569
00:43:12,381 --> 00:43:14,258
Big Issue!

570
00:43:15,509 --> 00:43:17,511
Big Issue!

571
00:43:17,845 --> 00:43:22,266
You think it'll last forever, people and cars and concrete.

572
00:43:23,100 --> 00:43:25,102
But it won't.

573
00:43:25,185 --> 00:43:27,229
One day, it's all gone.

574
00:43:28,188 --> 00:43:29,773
Even the sky.

575
00:43:36,697 --> 00:43:38,449
My planet's gone.

576
00:43:39,825 --> 00:43:41,368
It's dead.

577
00:43:43,829 --> 00:43:45,789
It burned, like the Earth.

578
00:43:46,290 --> 00:43:48,417
It's just rocks and dust.

579
00:43:50,002 --> 00:43:51,837
Before its time.

580
00:43:53,756 --> 00:43:55,090
What happened?

581
00:43:57,301 --> 00:44:00,012
There was a war, and we lost.

582
00:44:00,095 --> 00:44:02,014
A war with who?

583
00:44:05,684 --> 00:44:07,603
What about your people?

584
00:44:09,146 --> 00:44:11,190
I'm a Time Lord.

585
00:44:11,273 --> 00:44:13,651
I'm the last of the Time Lords.

586
00:44:14,443 --> 00:44:17,863
They're all gone. I'm the only survivor.

587
00:44:19,907 --> 00:44:22,159
I'm left travelling on my own 'cause there's no-one else.

588
00:44:23,994 --> 00:44:25,371
There's me.

589
00:44:29,291 --> 00:44:32,169
You've seen how dangerous it is. Do you wanna go home?

590
00:44:36,382 --> 00:44:37,925
I don't know.

591
00:44:39,551 --> 00:44:41,387
I want...

592
00:44:44,598 --> 00:44:46,892
Oh. Can you smell chips?

593
00:44:47,726 --> 00:44:51,105
- Yeah! Yeah. - I want chips.

594
00:44:51,355 --> 00:44:52,481
Me too!

595
00:44:52,564 --> 00:44:55,818
All right then, before you can get me in that box, chips it is and you can pay.

596
00:44:56,568 --> 00:44:59,738
- No money. - What sort of date are you?

597
00:44:59,822 --> 00:45:01,865
Come on then, tightwad. Chips are on me.

598
00:45:03,409 --> 00:45:05,828
We've only got five billion years till the shops close.

599
00:45:16,505 --> 00:45:18,799
Now, you've seen the future, so let's have a look at the past.

600
00:45:18,882 --> 00:45:21,218
1860. How does 1860 sound?

601
00:45:21,301 --> 00:45:23,721
- What happened in 1860? - I don't know! Let's find out.

602
00:45:25,514 --> 00:45:26,807
I can't believe she's gone.

603
00:45:26,890 --> 00:45:30,644
Not gone, Mr Redpath, sir. Merely sleeping.

604
00:45:31,603 --> 00:45:33,772
She's up and on her feet and out there somewhere!

605
00:45:33,856 --> 00:45:37,359
Mr Sneed, for shame, how many more times? It's ungodly!

606
00:45:38,569 --> 00:45:40,612
Excuse me, sir. Mr Dickens, this is your call.

607
00:45:41,029 --> 00:45:45,617
Use the sight. Find the old lady or you're dismissed.

608
00:45:46,160 --> 00:45:49,329
What phantasmagoria is this?

609
00:45:51,248 --> 00:45:52,583
That's more like it!

1
00:00:04,462 --> 00:00:05,505
วิ่ง.

2
00:00:08,842 --> 00:00:10,301
เอ่อ ผมชื่อหมอครับ คุณชื่ออะไรครับ

3
00:00:10,427 --> 00:00:13,096
- โรส - ยินดีที่ได้รู้จักนะ โรส วิ่งหนีเอาชีวิตรอดซะ!

4
00:00:19,269 --> 00:00:20,854
มันจะตามเรามา!

5
00:00:20,937 --> 00:00:23,314
กองทัพของเจงกีสข่านที่รวมตัวกันไม่สามารถผ่านประตูบานนั้นไปได้

6
00:00:23,398 --> 00:00:24,774
และเชื่อฉันเถอะว่าพวกเขาพยายามแล้ว

7
00:00:24,858 --> 00:00:27,068
- คุณเป็นมนุษย์ต่างดาวเหรอ? - ใช่ครับ.

8
00:00:30,989 --> 00:00:32,073
คุณสามารถมาด้วยกับฉันได้

9
00:00:32,157 --> 00:00:34,409
- มันอันตรายแบบนี้เสมอไปเหรอ? - ใช่.

10
00:00:41,458 --> 00:00:43,918
ใช่แล้ว โรส ไทเลอร์ คุณบอกฉันหน่อยสิว่าคุณอยากไปที่ไหน?

11
00:00:44,002 --> 00:00:48,298
ย้อนเวลาหรือเดินหน้า? อยู่ที่คุณเลือก แล้วจะเป็นยังไง?

12
00:00:49,841 --> 00:00:51,009
เดินหน้า.

13
00:00:55,805 --> 00:00:58,600
- ไกลแค่ไหน? - หนึ่งร้อยปี.

14
00:01:09,277 --> 00:01:12,447
ไปเลย! ก้าวออกจากประตูนั่นไป นี่มันศตวรรษที่ 22 แล้วนะ

15
00:01:12,614 --> 00:01:14,157
- คุณล้อเล่นนะ - แต่ว่ามันค่อนข้างน่าเบื่อนะ

16
00:01:14,240 --> 00:01:15,325
คุณอยากไปต่อไหม?

17
00:01:15,492 --> 00:01:16,659
ฉันก็สบายดี

18
00:01:24,834 --> 00:01:27,253
ในอนาคตอีกหนึ่งหมื่นปีข้างหน้า

19
00:01:27,337 --> 00:01:31,674
ก้าวออกไปข้างนอก นี่คือปี 12005 จักรวรรดิโรมันใหม่

20
00:01:31,758 --> 00:01:33,635
คุณคิดว่าคุณน่าประทับใจมาก

21
00:01:33,718 --> 00:01:35,887
- ฉันประทับใจมากเลย - คุณหวังนะ!

22
00:01:36,221 --> 00:01:39,724
เอาล่ะ คุณขอมา ฉันรู้ดีว่าต้องไปที่ไหน

23
00:01:43,228 --> 00:01:44,437
เดี๋ยว!

24
00:02:00,286 --> 00:02:02,038
เราอยู่ที่ไหน?

25
00:02:04,582 --> 00:02:06,334
มีอะไรอยู่ที่นั่น?

26
00:02:37,407 --> 00:02:41,619
พวกคุณ...พวกคุณใช้เวลาทั้งหมดไปกับการคิดถึงเรื่องความตาย

27
00:02:41,703 --> 00:02:46,416
คุณจะโดนฆ่าด้วยไข่ เนื้อวัว ภาวะโลกร้อน หรือดาวเคราะห์น้อยได้อย่างไร

28
00:02:47,083 --> 00:02:49,961
แต่คุณไม่เคยมีเวลาที่จะจินตนาการถึงสิ่งที่เป็นไปไม่ได้เลย

29
00:02:50,044 --> 00:02:51,796
บางทีคุณอาจจะรอดมาได้

30
00:02:54,132 --> 00:02:57,969
นี่คือปี 5.5/Apple/26

31
00:02:58,052 --> 00:03:00,138
ห้าพันล้านปีในอนาคตของคุณ

32
00:03:00,847 --> 00:03:02,765
และนี่ก็คือวันที่...

33
00:03:02,974 --> 00:03:04,392
เดี๋ยว...

34
00:03:11,608 --> 00:03:13,735
วันนี้เป็นวันที่ดวงอาทิตย์ขยายตัว

35
00:03:15,653 --> 00:03:18,031
ยินดีต้อนรับสู่จุดสิ้นสุดของโลก

36
00:04:09,707 --> 00:04:12,794
รถรับส่งหมายเลข 5 และ 6 กำลังจอดเทียบท่าแล้ว

37
00:04:13,878 --> 00:04:15,880
ขอเตือนแขกว่า Platform One

38
00:04:15,964 --> 00:04:19,676
ห้ามใช้อาวุธ การเทเลพอร์ต และห้ามนับถือศาสนา

39
00:04:20,677 --> 00:04:23,680
กำหนดการมรณะโลกคือ 15:39 น.

40
00:04:23,763 --> 00:04:26,641
ตามด้วยเครื่องดื่มในห้องแมนเชสเตอร์สวีท

41
00:04:27,392 --> 00:04:30,228
แล้วที่ว่า “แขก” หมายถึงคนใช่ไหมครับ?

42
00:04:30,311 --> 00:04:31,771
ขึ้นอยู่กับว่าคุณหมายถึงคนแบบไหน

43
00:04:31,854 --> 00:04:34,732
- ฉันหมายถึงคนนะ คุณหมายถึงอะไร - มนุษย์ต่างดาว

44
00:04:35,608 --> 00:04:38,653
พวกเขาทำอะไรอยู่บนยานอวกาศลำนี้กันนะ? ทั้งหมดนี้เพื่ออะไร?

45
00:04:38,736 --> 00:04:41,823
จริงๆ แล้วมันไม่ใช่ยานอวกาศหรอก มันเหมือนเป็นจุดชมวิวมากกว่า

46
00:04:41,906 --> 00:04:44,951
ผู้ยิ่งใหญ่และผู้ดีกำลังรวมตัวกันเพื่อเฝ้าดูโลกกำลังลุกไหม้

47
00:04:45,034 --> 00:04:46,661
- เพื่ออะไร? - สนุก!

48
00:04:50,540 --> 00:04:54,294
โปรดทราบว่าเมื่อฉันพูดว่า "ผู้ยิ่งใหญ่และคนดี" สิ่งที่ฉันหมายถึงก็คือคนรวย

49
00:04:54,377 --> 00:04:59,090
แต่... เดี๋ยวก่อน พวกเขาเคยทำแบบนี้ใน Newsround Extra เมื่อดวงอาทิตย์ขยายตัว

50
00:04:59,173 --> 00:05:01,676
- นั่นใช้เวลาหลายร้อยปี - ล้าน.

51
00:05:01,759 --> 00:05:03,803
แต่ปัจจุบันโลกนี้เป็นทรัพย์สินขององค์กร National Trust

52
00:05:03,886 --> 00:05:05,013
พวกเขาเก็บรักษามันเอาไว้

53
00:05:05,096 --> 00:05:08,933
เห็นข้างล่างนั่นไหม ดาวเทียมแรงโน้มถ่วงกำลังกั้นดวงอาทิตย์ไว้

54
00:05:09,767 --> 00:05:11,227
โลกก็ยังคงมีลักษณะเหมือนเดิม

55
00:05:11,311 --> 00:05:13,521
ฉันคิดว่าทวีปมีการเปลี่ยนแปลงและสิ่งต่างๆ

56
00:05:13,604 --> 00:05:16,733
พวกเขาทำแบบนั้น และทรัสต์ก็ย้ายพวกเขากลับไป! นั่นแหละโลกคลาสสิก

57
00:05:16,816 --> 00:05:19,902
แต่ตอนนี้เงินหมดแล้ว ธรรมชาติเข้ามาแทนที่

58
00:05:20,945 --> 00:05:22,238
นานแค่ไหนแล้ว?

59
00:05:23,197 --> 00:05:25,700
ประมาณครึ่งชั่วโมง แล้วดาวเคราะห์ก็ถูกเผา

60
00:05:26,409 --> 00:05:29,996
นั่นคือเหตุผลที่เราอยู่ที่นี่เหรอ? ฉันหมายถึง นั่นคือสิ่งที่คุณทำเหรอ?

61
00:05:30,079 --> 00:05:32,498
กระโจนเข้ามาในนาทีสุดท้ายและช่วยโลกใช่ไหม?

62
00:05:32,582 --> 00:05:34,917
ฉันไม่ได้เก็บมันไว้ หมดเวลาแล้ว

63
00:05:35,418 --> 00:05:39,005
- แล้วคนล่ะ? - ว่างเปล่า หายไปหมดแล้ว

64
00:05:43,259 --> 00:05:45,928
- แค่ฉันคนเดียว - คุณเป็นใครวะ?

65
00:05:46,054 --> 00:05:49,057
- โอ้ ดีจัง ขอบคุณนะ - แต่คุณเข้ามาได้ยังไง?

66
00:05:49,390 --> 00:05:51,851
ที่นี่เป็นโซนที่ให้การต้อนรับอย่างสูงสุด

67
00:05:51,934 --> 00:05:54,604
แขกลงจากเรือแล้ว! กำลังจะออกเดินทางในอีกไม่ช้า...

68
00:05:54,729 --> 00:05:57,106
ไม่นะ! นั่นฉันเอง ฉันเป็นแขกนะ ดูสิ ฉันได้รับคำเชิญ

69
00:05:57,231 --> 00:05:59,275
ดูสิ เห็นมั้ย ไม่เป็นไรนะ เห็นมั้ย

70
00:05:59,359 --> 00:06:00,443
"หมอ บวกหนึ่ง"

71
00:06:00,526 --> 00:06:03,029
ฉันเป็นหมอ ฉันชื่อโรส ไทเลอร์ เธอคือ "บวกหนึ่ง" ของฉัน

72
00:06:03,112 --> 00:06:04,530
แบบนี้โอเคมั้ย?

73
00:06:04,614 --> 00:06:06,449
ก็ชัดเจนอยู่แล้ว

74
00:06:07,784 --> 00:06:09,369
การขอโทษ ฯลฯ

75
00:06:09,452 --> 00:06:12,205
หากคุณอยู่บนเรือแล้ว เราควรเริ่มกันเลยดีกว่า

76
00:06:13,414 --> 00:06:15,083
สนุก.

77
00:06:16,292 --> 00:06:19,629
หนังสือพิมพ์นี้ค่อนข้างมีพลังจิตนะ มันแสดงให้พวกเขาเห็นทุกอย่างที่ฉันอยากให้พวกเขาเห็น

78
00:06:19,921 --> 00:06:21,631
ช่วยประหยัดเวลาได้มาก

79
00:06:21,756 --> 00:06:23,800
- เขาเป็นสีฟ้า - ใช่.

80
00:06:23,966 --> 00:06:25,051
ตกลง.

81
00:06:25,134 --> 00:06:28,888
เรามีคุณหมอและโรส ไทเลอร์มาร่วมด้วย!

82
